# File Organization & Naming Conventions

## Directory Structure
```
/
├── api/                    # Serverless API functions
├── components/             # React components
│   └── ui/                # Advanced/specialized UI components
├── hooks/                 # Custom React hooks
├── lib/                   # Utility functions and helpers
├── [root files]           # Main app files and configuration
```

## Naming Conventions
### Files & Directories
- **Components**: PascalCase (e.g., `JsonInput.tsx`, `LoadingSpinner.tsx`)
- **Hooks**: camelCase with `use` prefix (e.g., `useJsonProcessor.ts`)
- **Utilities**: camelCase (e.g., `utils.ts`, `jsonCollapse.ts`)
- **Constants**: camelCase (e.g., `constants.tsx`)
- **API**: kebab-case (e.g., `gemini-ai.js`)

### Code Elements
- **Variables**: camelCase (`formattedJson`, `isLoading`)
- **Functions**: camelCase (`processJson`, `handleInputChange`)
- **Components**: PascalCase (`JsonInput`, `AiLoadingIndicator`)
- **Types/Interfaces**: PascalCase (`JsonInputProps`, `OutputFormat`)
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (`GEMINI_MODEL_NAME`)

## File Responsibilities
### Component Files
Each component file should:
- Export a single main component
- Include related types/interfaces
- Contain component-specific sub-components
- Have minimal external dependencies

### Hook Files
Located in [hooks/](mdc:hooks/), each hook should:
- Have a single primary responsibility
- Export the hook function and related types
- Use descriptive parameter and return value names
- Include comprehensive TypeScript types

### Utility Files
Located in [lib/](mdc:lib/):
- [utils.ts](mdc:lib/utils.ts) - General utility functions
- [jsonCollapse.ts](mdc:lib/jsonCollapse.ts) - JSON structure parsing and collapsing

### Configuration Files
- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Dependencies and scripts
- [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json) - TypeScript configuration
- [vite.config.ts](mdc:vite.config.ts) - Build tool configuration
- [vercel.json](mdc:vercel.json) - Deployment configuration

## Import/Export Patterns
### Imports
```typescript
// External libraries first
import React, { useState, useCallback } from 'react';
import { clsx } from 'clsx';

// Internal imports with relative paths
import { JsonInput } from './components/JsonInput';
import { useJsonProcessor } from './hooks/useJsonProcessor';
import { cn } from './lib/utils';
```

### Exports
- Use **named exports** for components and utilities
- Export types and interfaces alongside components
- Group related exports at the end of files

## Special Files
- [metadata.json](mdc:metadata.json) - Application metadata
- [robots.txt](mdc:robots.txt) & [sitemap.xml](mdc:sitemap.xml) - SEO files
- [test-gemini.js](mdc:test-gemini.js) - AI integration testing
- [constants.cjs.js](mdc:constants.cjs.js) - CommonJS constants (legacy compatibility)
